d 'DBF2STATA': module for batch conversion of DBF files to Stata .dta format
d
d  dbf2stata is a Stata 16+ command for batch conversion of DBF
d files to Stata .dta format. The command uses the public dbf2stata
d Python package as its conversion engine and supports DBF date and
d datetime fields, numeric and logical fields, character and memo
d fields, lowercase variable names by default, optional
d preservation of DBF field-name case, selectable output
d directories, and overwrite protection. The package also includes
d dbf2stata_setup, a companion setup utility for the external
d Python dependency. dbf2stata itself never silently installs or
d upgrades Python packages. If the Python engine is missing, the
d user receives a clear message to run dbf2stata_setup. When
d explicitly invoked, dbf2stata_setup uses the exact Python
d interpreter currently running inside Stata, checks Python and
d pip, installs the supported public PyPI dependency when needed,
d and verifies that the conversion engine can be imported. 
d
d KW: DBF files
d KW: Python
d
d Requires: Stata version 16 and Python 3.10
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260820
d
d Author: William Dormechele,  University of East Anglia 
d Support: email W.Dormechele@@uea.ac.uk
d
f dbf2stata.ado
f dbf2stata.sthlp
f dbf2stata_setup.ado
f dbf2stata_setup.sthlp
